  "id": "bond",
  "term": "bond",
  "definition": "In developmental psychology, bond usually refers here to the mother–infant bond: a changing emotional relationship in which the mother responds suitably to the baby’s needs and experiences the baby’s signals positively. This bond helps create a secure, nurturing setting that supports the child’s development and later relationships.",
